  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "3. Method in 5 steps"
  },
  {
   "type": "li",
   "text": "Read the gross floor area (GO) of the building from BAG (section 4)."
  },
  {
   "type": "li",
   "text": "Assign a building type and construction cohort, giving a material profile (section 5)."
  },
  {
   "type": "li",
   "text": "Look up the 13 material intensities of that profile in Tabel B2 (section 6)."
  },
  {
   "type": "li",
   "text": "Calculate each material mass: quantity = GO x intensity (section 7)."
  },
  {
   "type": "li",
   "text": "Calculate CO2 per material: CO2 = mass x emission factor, then add up (section 8)."
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "4. Step 1 - Gross floor area from BAG"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "GO is the only measured number per building. It is the sum of the usable floor area of every dwelling unit (verblijfsobject) in the pand."
  },
