  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "14. Limits"
  },
  {
   "type": "li",
   "text": "The estimate scales with floor area only. A tall hall and a low hall with the same GO get the same materials."
  },
  {
   "type": "li",
   "text": "B2 intensities are national averages per type and cohort, not the construction of the individual building."
  },
  {
   "type": "li",
   "text": "The type mapping is coarse: assembly, healthcare, hotel, sports and education all become 'overig'."
  },
  {
   "type": "li",
   "text": "Overige constructie mineralen dominates the mass (sand, gravel, mortar) and carries a 0.50 factor, which makes it the largest single CO2 source."
  },
  {
   "type": "li",
   "text": "Copper, aluminium and other metal do not use the same factor in every row (section 8)."
  },
  {
   "type": "li",
   "text": "Emission factors are coarse working values; replace with Nationale Milieudatabase values for official reporting."
  },
